<h2 local-id=3D"620ebf1124b3" id=3D"FIONA_IntegrationFailureManagement_BRD_=
V1.0-1.ExecutiveSummary">1. Executive Summary</h2>
<p local-id=3D"4947d183d162">The Finance Systems team currently manages int=
egration failures using a macro-based Excel workbook alongside email commun=
ication between teams. This approach is inefficient, difficult to manage at=
 scale, and does not provide clear or consistent visibility of failure stat=
us or progress.</p>
<p local-id=3D"8df51af0a6f3">To address these challenges, a new <strong>Int=
egration Failures Management Module</strong> will be developed within the F=
IONA platform. This module will provide a structured and centralised approa=
ch to logging, tracking, and resolving integration failures across all fail=
ure types.</p>
<p local-id=3D"caab0c69da6c">The solution will introduce:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"2a060200-8517-45cb-ac6b-9aa78a326b47">
<li local-id=3D"db62fb7b-797b-450c-8ad8-7a41e7239f3d">
<p local-id=3D"76bf896ee7fc">A standardised method for capturing failures</=
p></li>
<li local-id=3D"3c6d4763-c174-497c-b0e5-1dcf3dc790c1">
<p local-id=3D"24496701e36b">Clear ownership at each stage of the process</=
p></li>
<li local-id=3D"41fa82f7-8cba-449a-8bcf-15f257667d77">
<p local-id=3D"f8bb7150a54e">Defined status tracking to monitor progress</p=
></li>
<li local-id=3D"d33ca197-86d9-4c23-bfb8-4b67ab74a4a0">
<p local-id=3D"248989a4ff6b">Controlled and consistent communication throug=
h system-generated notifications</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"9d2ecd98-c0a3-465c-b57c-89d010944ab1">
<p local-id=3D"419ab86596f2">Improved visibility of failures and their curr=
ent state</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"11e4681d-7787-4562-b8ba-6cdd3468eb94">
<p local-id=3D"2e7b92201af8">A foundation for reporting and analysis</p></l=
i>
</ul>
<h2 local-id=3D"927358210134" id=3D"FIONA_IntegrationFailureManagement_BRD_=
V1.0-2.BusinessContext&amp;Background">2. Business Context &amp; Background=
</h2>
<p local-id=3D"33fd6b8e2eac">The Finance Systems team supports integrations=
 between multiple operational systems (such as Columbus, One Step, Nexum, F=
leet, Genesis, and Exodus) and Microsoft Dynamics 365 (D365).</p>
<p local-id=3D"23fad28131e1">When files are processed in D365, the system p=
erforms validation checks against predefined lookup (translation) tables. I=
f required mappings are missing or invalid, the file fails and requires inv=
estigation and resolution.</p>
<p local-id=3D"965f91518a5f">At present:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"12e74949-ebb2-4a3c-975c-4f63d6198b7b">
<li local-id=3D"61c2a04b-22e1-4cab-ae85-70b17534fced">
<p local-id=3D"baa2b396fe79">Integration failures are recorded using a comb=
ination of Excel and email communication</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"4f110c9f-639c-4896-8dc5-4ffa938b0d60">
<p local-id=3D"39beee3b7380">Information related to failures is maintained =
across multiple sources rather than a single system</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"59b9cd89-c88e-4598-b636-5fec45a9bdb4">
<p local-id=3D"9f7a0f293b27">The process relies on manual updates and follo=
w-ups</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"da253ef0-af0f-46eb-8037-42c29649b83f">
<p local-id=3D"5cdf4f444349">Tracking the current status of a failure requi=
res manual effort and is not immediately visible</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"7f9d1df4-bd7b-4e6f-90f5-16f343c782e7">
<p local-id=3D"e685d373d9f1">Ownership and progress of individual failures =
are not consistently tracked within a single workflow</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"603c9c4efb7e">This results in inefficiencies and makes it di=
fficult to gain a clear, real-time view of integration failures and their r=
esolution status.</p>
<h2 local-id=3D"ac325b3bd8e6" id=3D"FIONA_IntegrationFailureManagement_BRD_=
V1.0-3.Scope">3. Scope</h2>
<h3 local-id=3D"84a571baea53" id=3D"FIONA_IntegrationFailureManagement_BRD_=
V1.0-3.1InScope">3.1&nbsp; In Scope</h3>
<ul local-id=3D"0014d47013e3">
<li local-id=3D"d2eada45fe6d">
<p local-id=3D"f81e3ad1bff2">A new Integration Failures module within the F=
IONA platform</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"7e445faec024">
<p local-id=3D"fa246eef2afd">A structured failure data capture form for use=
 by Finance Systems technicians</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"8344b51bd373">
<p local-id=3D"2d6895b6d6be">A record log displaying all open and closed fa=
ilure records</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"efff5394271b">
<p local-id=3D"9cafb8809f71">A defined status workflow with two distinct pa=
ths:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"e4a766f39fde">
<li local-id=3D"57029d0b9f82">
<p local-id=3D"447fa3834b6d">Full path (Open =E2=86=92 With Masterdata =E2=
=86=92 With Finance Systems =E2=86=92 Closed) for translation and on-hold f=
ailure types,</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"e3f084a76e15">
<p local-id=3D"0f8958b42ed9">short path (Open =E2=86=92 With Finance System=
s =E2=86=92 Closed) for failures handled internally by Finance Systems.</p>=
</li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"8406bd8243d6">
<p local-id=3D"05bca124366b">Automated email notification to <a class=3D"ex=
ternal-link" href=3D"mailto:masterdata@marstonholdings.co.uk" rel=3D"nofoll=
ow">masterdata@marstonholdings.co.uk</a> for applicable failure types</p></=
li>
<li local-id=3D"7c8b250802c0">
<p local-id=3D"f308d83c3d47">Portal access for the Masterdata team to view =
all records and edit records within their applicable failure types</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"55b225d5d9f0">
<p local-id=3D"83ee096522ad">Ability for reopening of closed records with A=
pproval.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"0eb08f94a294">
<p local-id=3D"587a2d00984e">All eight failure types as defined in Section =
2.1</p></li>
</ul>
<h3 local-id=3D"fc7b9042171e" id=3D"FIONA_IntegrationFailureManagement_BRD_=
V1.0-3.2OutofScope">3.2&nbsp; Out of Scope</h3>
<ul local-id=3D"9ad35a40506d">
<li local-id=3D"4f10de9e3141">
<p local-id=3D"dcd9be4a8cba">Migration of historical data from the existing=
 macro workbook</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"a080c0fb33f5">
<p local-id=3D"688cd22b0c5b">Integration with external ticketing systems</p=
></li>
<li local-id=3D"31e428de062f">
<p local-id=3D"c32eb9b91316">Automated resolution of failures</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"82aa75730552">
<p local-id=3D"b8b87bd25ddc">Changes to the D365 translation table configur=
ation process itself</p></li>
</ul>
